    {
      "id": "TE-C46-fruit",
      "sequence": 1130,
      "title": "పండు (paṇḍu) — a fruit",
      "headword": "పండు",
      "romanization": "paṇḍu",
      "gloss": "a fruit",
      "script": "telugu",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:6a95782cd5ffc734",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did bhārya mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పండు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పండు (paṇḍu) — \"a fruit\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పండు is also a verb: to ripen. The fruit is named for what happened to it — the ripened thing — and Telugu never troubled to invent a second noun. Say paṇḍu of a mango on the table and you mean the fruit; say it of the tree's crop and you mean it is coming ripe."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kannada writes the same inherited word ಹಣ್ಣು (haṇṇu). That p- at the front turning into h- is a regular Kannada sound law, and it has already turned up once, on పాలు beside ಹಾಲು. Watch for it again."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పండు (paṇḍu) is native Dravidian, one word with Tamil paḻu, \"to ripen\", and Kannada paṇṇu, \"ripe fruit\" (DEDR 4004). DEDR lists the Telugu as both \"to ripen\" and \"fruit\". DEDR compares Sanskrit phala, \"fruit\" (CDIAL 9051)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five things you might ask someone for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "paṇḍu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *paṇḍu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "paṇḍu, then dayacēsi paṇḍu ivvaṇḍi — \"please give a fruit\"",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *paṇḍu*, then *dayacēsi paṇḍu ivvaṇḍi* — \"please give a fruit\"]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does పండు (paṇḍu) mean? (\"a fruit\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
