          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: దీపం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దీపం (dīpaṁ) — \"a lamp\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దీపం (dīpaṁ) is the small clay lamp with oil and a wick. Its Sanskrit root dīp means \"to blaze\", so the word names the burning rather than the vessel."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Put దీప together with a word meaning \"a row\" and you get dīpāvaḷi, \"a row of lamps\" — the festival English spells Diwali. The ending is the tatsama neuter -ం, the same shape already carried by హృదయం and భోజనం."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "CDIAL 6348 lists Sanskrit dīpa, \"lamp\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three: a fruit, a cloth, a lamp."
            }
          ]
        },
