        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ఉప్పు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఉప్పు (uppu) — \"salt\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Proto-Dravidian had uppu, and the whole family kept it almost untouched: Tamil உப்பு, Kannada ಉಪ್ಪು, Malayalam ഉപ്പ്. A word this ordinary gives nobody a reason to replace it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Notice the doubled ప్ప in the middle. Telugu likes a consonant twice inside a short word — కుక్క, పిల్లి, కన్ను all do it — and the doubling is not decoration: it is the difference between one word and another."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "DEDR 2674 lists Telugu uppu, \"salt\", with Tamil uppu, Kannada uppu and Malayalam uppu."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four. Three of them inherited, one borrowed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
