        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పుస్తకం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పుస్తకం (pustakaṁ) — \"a book\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit pustaka is the source, but the trail behind it leaves India altogether. Middle Persian post meant \"hide, skin\" — the thing written on before paper."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So the Telugu word for a book carries an animal skin folded up inside it, and it arrived by the same north-western road as రోజు, which turned out to be Persian too. Two of these five walked in from outside; three were always here."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "CDIAL 8413 takes Sanskrit pustaka from Iranian, comparing Sogdian pwstk, \"book\", and Persian pōst, \"skin\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five things you might ask for: a fruit, a cloth, a lamp, salt, a book."
            }
          ]
        },
